\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Full modelling framework. Centre: the six-stage pipeline, estimated on HHTS diaries ($\sim $20,000 persons) and applied to the 3.82-million-person synthetic population across 371 SA2 zones --- from CDAP (Stage~0) through activity frequency, day budget, duration and timing (Stages~1--4) to joint tour mode $\times $ destination choice (Stage~5m/5d: two-level nested logit, MNL over Manski--Lerman-sampled zones, PLC-captivity and M3 schedule-set arms), detour-feasible intermediate-stop destinations (Stage~5b), predict-only validation and repair (Stage~6), and export to DynusT/MATSim-ready plans. \textbf  {Levels:} the left rail separates tour level (Stages~0--5, blue: whole-tour decisions, including the tour's single main mode and its destination) from trip level (Stages~5b--6, teal: the individual legs and intermediate stops inside each tour); the inset states the distinction. Left: data inputs. Right: the P1 crash chain (100~m segments, SPF search, Empirical Bayes, OD accumulation) yielding the \texttt  {CRASH} skim consumed by Stage~5 and the home crash-accessibility index offered to Stages~0--1. Bottom: the P2 SparseEA-AGDS search, which specifies every stage, against the P0 fixed comparison arm (published specifications, maximum likelihood, universal choice sets); shared calibration $\mathcal  {K}$ and the held-out validation block implement the (P0)-versus-(P2) error comparison. Amber dashed: safety terms entering the utilities. Grey dashed: skim feedback from the generated plans into the Stage-5 skims. Skims are $371\times 371$ OD matrices --- travel time [min], monetary cost [\$], distance [km] and \texttt  {CRASH} [expected crashes accumulated per OD path]; the home-zone crash-accessibility index is in log units per origin, and mode logsums are in log-utility units per tour--zone.}}{3}{figure.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:pipeline}{{1}{3}{Full modelling framework. Centre: the six-stage pipeline, estimated on HHTS diaries ($\sim $20,000 persons) and applied to the 3.82-million-person synthetic population across 371 SA2 zones --- from CDAP (Stage~0) through activity frequency, day budget, duration and timing (Stages~1--4) to joint tour mode $\times $ destination choice (Stage~5m/5d: two-level nested logit, MNL over Manski--Lerman-sampled zones, PLC-captivity and M3 schedule-set arms), detour-feasible intermediate-stop destinations (Stage~5b), predict-only validation and repair (Stage~6), and export to DynusT/MATSim-ready plans. \textbf {Levels:} the left rail separates tour level (Stages~0--5, blue: whole-tour decisions, including the tour's single main mode and its destination) from trip level (Stages~5b--6, teal: the individual legs and intermediate stops inside each tour); the inset states the distinction. Left: data inputs. Right: the P1 crash chain (100~m segments, SPF search, Empirical Bayes, OD accumulation) yielding the \texttt {CRASH} skim consumed by Stage~5 and the home crash-accessibility index offered to Stages~0--1. Bottom: the P2 SparseEA-AGDS search, which specifies every stage, against the P0 fixed comparison arm (published specifications, maximum likelihood, universal choice sets); shared calibration $\mathcal {K}$ and the held-out validation block implement the (P0)-versus-(P2) error comparison. Amber dashed: safety terms entering the utilities. Grey dashed: skim feedback from the generated plans into the Stage-5 skims. Skims are $371\times 371$ OD matrices --- travel time [min], monetary cost [\$], distance [km] and \texttt {CRASH} [expected crashes accumulated per OD path]; the home-zone crash-accessibility index is in log units per origin, and mode logsums are in log-utility units per tour--zone}{figure.caption.3}{}}
\newlabel{fig:pipeline@cref}{{[figure][1][]1}{[1][2][]3}{}{}{}}
